    "field": "Arctic paleoceanography",
    "problem": "The Cenozoic climate history of the Arctic Ocean has been virtually unknown because the extreme challenge of drilling through heavy sea ice has limited previous sediment core recovery to only the uppermost, most recent few meters, preventing deeper paleoenvironmental reconstruction.",
    "method": "To solve the challenge of drilling in heavy sea ice, the expedition used a fleet of two icebreakers to continuously break upstream ice floes, allowing a drilling vessel to maintain a fixed position and recover deep sediment cores from the central Arctic Ocean.",
    "task": "The task is to recover and analyze the first deep sediment cores from the central Arctic Ocean to reconstruct the region's paleoceanographic and climatic history throughout the Cenozoic era.",
